7. Student Performance Trend Analysis

1. Problem Statement
Compare student scores across three assessments, calculate changes,
identify subjects consistently below a defined threshold, and classify the overall trend.

2. Objectives
•	Calculate improvement or decline between assessments.
•	Identify consistently weak subjects.
•	Classify performance using average marks.

3. Assumptions
•	Scores are out of 100.
•	The dataset contains three assessments per subject.
•	A subject is consistently weak if all three scores are below 40.
•	Average ≥ 75 is High, ≥ 50 is Moderate, otherwise Needs Improvement.

4. Algorithm
1. Store subject scores as nested lists.
2. Calculate change from first to last assessment.
3. Check for consistently weak subjects.
4. Calculate overall average and classify.
5. Print a summary.

5. Flowchart
       (START)
          |
    Enter Subject Marks
          |
  Calculate Score Changes
          |
   Check Marks < 40
          |
  Calculate Average
          |
  Check Performance
          |
  Print Result and Weak Subjects
          |
        (STOP)

6. Pseudocode
BEGIN
INPUT product price and quantity
CALCULATE total amount
IF total >= 1000, APPLY 10% discount
